,                                                 \'SBAYRAKTAR\',                                                 \'SDESEN\',                                                 \'SEONEY\',                                                 \'SKIZILKAYA\',                                                 \'SOFLAS\',                                                 \'SOZORAL\',                                                 \'SSAROHAN\',                                                 \'SSUSLER\',                                                 \'TAKTURK\',                                                 \'TKASDAS\',                                                 \'TSAYAN\',                                                 \'TUVURAL\',                                                 \'UEMRE\',                                                 \'VDEMIR\',                                                 \'YBOZCAM\'))          AND PRIVILEGE  not in ( \'SELECT\',\'READ\',\'EXECUTE\')','Developers and analysts are correctly granted to roles\r','Developers and analysts are no correctly granted to  roles Revoke the grants mentioned in detail part','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:43:15'),(244,202601,7,46,'AA_Oracle_010_SQL92_SECURITY_True','major','OTHER','The SQL92_SECURITY parameter setting TRUE requires that a user must also be granted the SELECT object privilege before being able to perform UPDATE or DELETE operations on tables that have WHERE or SET clauses. The setting should have a value of TRUE.   CIS Oracle Database 2.2.16','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SQL92_SECURITY\' and UPPER(VALUE) =\'TRUE\'','== 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SQL92_SECURITY\'','The SQL92_SECURITY  parameter value is acceptable\r\n','The SQL92_SECURITY  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be TRUE','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:43:15'),(245,202601,7,49,'AA_Oracle_040_O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY_False','major','OTHER','This test checks the value of the O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY parameter.  Oracle 8 provides the parameter O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY to prevent accounts with the privilege SELECT ANY TABLE from selecting the data dictionary tables. Setting this parameter to FALSE helps restrict access to sensitive data in the data dictionary such as the encrypted passwords.    CIS 2.2.10','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY\' and UPPER(VALUE) =\'FALSE\'','== 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY\'','The O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY parameter value is acceptable\r\n','The O7_DICTIONARY_ACCESSIBILITY  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be FALSE','fail',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:43:15'),(246,202601,7,54,'AA_Oracle_090__TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC_False','major','OTHER','This test checks the value of the _TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC parameter.  The _TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC parameter is used to make trace files used for debugging database applications and events available to all database users. Use of this capability precludes the discrete assignment of privileges based on job function.  Additionally, its use may provide access to external files and data to unauthorized users. The value for the _TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC parameter by default is false when it is not set.   If the parameter does not exist or is set to FALSE, this is not a finding.      CIS 2.2.17','','select sum(a) from    ( SELECT count(*) a   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME) = \'_TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC\'    union all   SELECT count(*) a   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'_TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC\' and value=\'FALSE\')','!= 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'_TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC\'','The _TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC parameter value is acceptable\r\n','The _TRACE_FILES_PUBLIC  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be FALSE  or must n