OLES                               WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')   AND GRANTEE not in (\'MF_DBSPI\',\'GDENT\',\'HP_DBSPI\',\'UCMDBDISC\',\'GDMMONITOR\',\'SRV_DEVICE42\')   AND GRANTEE not like \'APEX%\'','The  privileges for some SYS views are correctly set \r','The  privileges for some SYS  views are not correctly set ','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:52:35'),(303,202601,8,71,'AA_Oracle_200_12_SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON_True','major','OTHER','This test checks the value of the SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON parameter. Enablement of password case sensitivity allows Oracle password complexity to meet DoD password requirements. Password complexity decreases the likelihood of successful password attacks by malicious users. This parameter should be TRUE   CIS Oracle Database 2.2.11','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON\' and UPPER(VALUE) =\'TRUE\'','== 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON\'','The SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON parameter value is acceptable\r','The SEC_CASE_SENSITIVE_LOGON  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be TRUE','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:52:35'),(304,202601,8,72,'AA_Oracle_210_SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS _Set_3','major','OTHER','SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS specifies the number of authentication attempts that can be made by a client on a connection to the server process.  After the specified number of failure attempts, the connection will be automatically dropped by the server process.  An unlimited number of login attempts for a user connection can facilitate both brute-force login attacks and the occurrence of Denial-of-Service.  The SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS parameter should be set between 1 to 3 according to the STIG and CIS recommendations.  The Guardium recommended default threshold is 3.  The threshold can be adjusted to a higher or lower value to accommodate your organizational needs.   CIS Oracle Database   2.2.12','','SELECT to_number(value)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS\'','<= 3','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS\'','The SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS parameter value is acceptable\r','The SEC_MAX_FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be  3 or less','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:52:35'),(305,202601,8,73,'AA_Oracle_220_SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION _Set_Drop_3','major','OTHER','The database is vulnerable to exhaustion of resources that could result in a Denial of Service (DoS) to other clients if not protected from a flood of bad packets submitted by a malicious or errant client connection. The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION initialization parameter should be set to  DROP,3 acceptance of bad packets from a client in order to support the continued function of other non-problematic connections   CIS Oracle Database   2.2.13','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION\' and    UPPER(VALUE) in (\'(DROP,3)\')','== 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION\'','The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION parameter value is acceptable\r','The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_FURTHER_ACTION  parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be  (DROP, 3)  or less','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:52:35'),(306,202601,8,74,'AA_Oracle_230_SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION _Set_LOG','major','OTHER','Undetected attacks using bad packets can lead to a successful Denial of Service (DoS) to database clients. Notification of attacks based on a flood of bad packets sent to the database can assist in discovery and response to this type of attack.  The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION parameter, specifies the action that the database should take when bad packets are received from a possibly malicious client.  The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION  parameter should be set to LOG   CIS Oracle Database   2.2.14','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION\'  and UPPER(VALUE) =\'LOG\'','== 1','','SELECT  UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION\'  and UPPER(VALUE) =\'LOG\'','The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION parameter value is acceptable\r','The SEC_PROTOCOL_ERROR_TRACE_ACTION   parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be  LOG','fail',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-03 08:52:35'),(307,202601,8,75,'AA_Oracle_240_11_Oracle default tablespace assignment','major','OTHER','The Oracle SYSTEM and SYSAUX  tablespace is used by the database to store all DBMS system objects. Other use of the system tablespace may compromise system availability and the effectiveness of host system access controls to the tablespace files.  This test excludes default object owners from a predefined Guardium group called \"Oracle exclude default system grantees\".','','SELECT  count(*)     FROM dba_users    WHERE       default_tablespace IN (\'SYSTEM\', \'SYSAUX\') AND     username NOT IN   (   \'MF_DBSPI\',   \'ANONYMOUS\',   \'CTXSYS\',   \'DBSNMP\',   \'EXFSYS\',   \'LBACSYS\',   \'MDSYS\',   \'MGMT_VIEW\',   \'OLAPSYS\',   \'OWBSYS\',   \'ORDPLUGINS\',   \'ORDSYS\',   \'OUTLN\',   \'SI_INFORMTN_SCHEMA\',   \'SYS\',   \'SYSMAN\',   \'SYSTEM\',   \'TSMSYS\',   \'WK_TEST\',   \'WKSYS\',   \'WKPROXY\',   \'WMSYS\',   \'XDB\',   \'APEX_PUBLIC_USER\',   \'DIP\',   \'FLOWS_30000\',   \'FLOWS_FILES\',   \'MDDATA\',   \'ORACLE_OCM\',   \'SPATIAL_CSW_ADMIN_USR\',   \'SPATIAL_WFS_ADMIN_USR\',   \'XS$NULL\',   \'OWBSYS_AUDIT\',   \'ORDDATA\',   \'APEX_030200\',   \'APPQOSSYS\',   \'DVSYS\',   \'DVF\',   \'CONNECT\',   \'RESOURCE\',   \'DBA\',   \'PDB_DBA\',   \'AUDIT_ADMIN\',   \'AUDIT_VIEWER\',   \'SELECT_CATALOG_ROLE\',   \'EXECUTE_CATALOG_ROLE\',   \'CAPTURE_ADMIN\',   \'EXP_FULL_DATABASE\',   \'IMP_FULL_DAT