'APEX%\'   ','Default Tablespaces are correctly set.\r','Default Tablespaces are  not correctly set. Some app user deafult tablespace is set to SYTEM or SYSAUX','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-16 15:16:26'),(1026,202601,26,76,'AA_Oracle_240_12_Oracle default tablespace assignment','major','CONFIG','The Oracle SYSTEM and SYSAUX  tablespace is used by the database to store all DBMS system objects. Other use of the system tablespace may compromise system availability and the effectiveness of host system access controls to the tablespace files.  This test excludes default object owners from a predefined Guardium group called \"Oracle exclude default system grantees\".','','SELECT  count(*)     FROM dba_users    WHERE     default_tablespace IN (\'SYSTEM\', \'SYSAUX\')          AND username NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                 FROM DBA_USERS                                WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')   AND username not like \'APEX%\'','== 0','','SELECT username||\'  \'||default_tablespace     FROM dba_users    WHERE     default_tablespace IN (\'SYSTEM\', \'SYSAUX\')          AND username NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                 FROM DBA_USERS                                WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')   AND username not like \'APEX%\'   ','Default Tablespaces are correctly set.\r','Default Tablespaces are  not correctly set. Some app user deafult tablespace is set to SYTEM or SYSAUX','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-16 15:16:26'),(1027,202601,26,45,'AA_Oracle_001_Version','critical','PATCH','This test cheks Database version whether is acceptable version.','\r\n','select count(substr(version,1,4)) from v$instance  where substr(version,1,4) > \'12.1\'','== 1','','select version from v$instance','The installed Oracle  version is in acceptable version\r\n','The installed Oracle  version is not acceptable version ; it  is recommended that you upgrade this oracle instance to  at least 12.2 or higher version.','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-16 15:16:26'),(1028,202601,26,100,'AA_Oracle_390_Limit External User Login Capability','minor','AUTH','This test checks for users with EXTERNAL authentication type. EXTERNAL authentication type can be authenticated by a remote OS to allow access to the database with full authorization.  Allowing remote OS authentication of a user to the database can potentially allow supposed \"privileged users\" to connect as \"authenticated,\" even when the remote system is compromised, these logins should be disabled or restricted according to the needs of your organization.   CIS 4.3    ','','SELECT count(*)    FROM DBA_USERS WHERE    AUTHENTICATION_TYPE = \'EXTERNAL\'','== 0','','SELECT USERNAME FROM DBA_USERS WHERE AUTHENTICATION_TYPE = \'EXTERNAL\'','There is no external user in this database\r','There are external users in this database. Drop them','pass',NULL,NULL,'2026-01-16 15:16:26'),(1029,202601,26,96,'AA_Oracle_370_11_Limit Roles Granted With ADMIN Option','major','PRIV','This test checks whether Oracle role privileges have been granted with the ADMIN option to grantees with no DBA role, which allows the grantees to make grants to other users.  The ADMIN option reduces administrative control and creates an unwarranted vulnerability.  This test excludes grantees from a predefined Guardium group called \"Oracle exclude default system grantees\".   ','','Select count(*)     FROM DBA_ROLE_PRIVS    WHERE     ADMIN_OPTION = \'YES\'    AND GRANTEE NOT IN  (   \'MF_DBSPI\',   \'ANONYMOUS\',   \'CTXSYS\',   \'DBSNMP\',   \'EXFSYS\',   \'LBACSYS\',   \'MDSYS\',   \'MGMT_VIEW\',   \'OLAPSYS\',   \'OWBSYS\',   \'ORDPLUGINS\',   \'ORDSYS\',   \'OUTLN\',   \'SI_INFORMTN_SCHEMA\',   \'SYS\',   \'SYSMAN\',   \'SYSTEM\',   \'TSMSYS\',   \'WK_TEST\',   \'WKSYS\',   \'WKPROXY\',   \'WMSYS\',   \'XDB\',   \'APEX_PUBLIC_USER\',   \'DIP\',   \'FLOWS_30000\',   \'FLOWS_FILES\',   \'MDDATA\',   \'ORACLE_OCM\',   \'SPATIAL_CSW_ADMIN_USR\',   \'SPATIAL_WFS_ADMIN_USR\',   \'XS$NULL\',   \'OWBSYS_AUDIT\',   \'