  \'DV_MONITOR\',   \'DV_STREAMS_ADMIN\',   \'DV_GOLDENGATE_ADMIN\',   \'DV_XSTREAM_ADMIN\',   \'DV_GOLDENGATE_REDO_ACCESS\',   \'DV_AUDIT_CLEANUP\',   \'DV_DATAPUMP_NETWORK_LINK\',   \'DV_POLICY_OWNER\',   \'DBSFWUSER\',   \'GGSYS\',   \'OJVMSYS\',   \'GSMADMIN_INTERNAL\',   \'SYS$UMF\'   )   AND username not like \'APEX%\'   ','Default Tablespaces are correctly set.\r','Default Tablespaces are  not correctly set. Some app user deafult tablespace is set to SYTEM or SYSAUX','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(76,'AA_Oracle_240_12_Oracle default tablespace assignment','oracle','major','CONFIG','The Oracle SYSTEM and SYSAUX  tablespace is used by the database to store all DBMS system objects. Other use of the system tablespace may compromise system availability and the effectiveness of host system access controls to the tablespace files.  This test excludes default object owners from a predefined Guardium group called \"Oracle exclude default system grantees\".','','SELECT  count(*)     FROM dba_users    WHERE     default_tablespace IN (\'SYSTEM\', \'SYSAUX\')          AND username NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                 FROM DBA_USERS                                WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')   AND username not like \'APEX%\'','== 0','','SELECT username||\'  \'||default_tablespace     FROM dba_users    WHERE     default_tablespace IN (\'SYSTEM\', \'SYSAUX\')          AND username NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                 FROM DBA_USERS                                WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')   AND username not like \'APEX%\'   ','Default Tablespaces are correctly set.\r','Default Tablespaces are  not correctly set. Some app user deafult tablespace is set to SYTEM or SYSAUX','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(77,'AA_Oracle_250_Default SID name','oracle','critical','CONFIG','Use of the default Oracle System Identifier (SID) leaves the database vulnerable to attacks that target Oracle installations running under default SID. Using a custom name helps protect the database against this kind of targeted attack.','','select count(*) from v$database where   name in (    \'XE\',	 	    \'IASDB\',		   \'ORCL\',		   \'OEMREP\',		   \'IXOS\',		   \'CTM4_0\',		   \'CTM4_1\',		   \'CTM4_6\',		   \'CTM4_7\',		   \'ARIS\',		   \'MSAM\',		   \'VPX\',	   \'OPENVIEW\',		   \'OVO\')	','== 0','','select name from v$database where   name in (    \'XE\',	 	    \'IASDB\',		   \'ORCL\',		   \'OEMREP\',		   \'IXOS\',		   \'CTM4_0\',		   \'CTM4_1\',		   \'CTM4_6\',		   \'CTM4_7\',		   \'ARIS\',		   \'MSAM\',		   \'VPX\',	   \'OPENVIEW\',		   \'OVO\')	','Database SID is properly set.\r','Database SID is not properly set. Default SID is used ','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(78,'AA_Oracle_260_SEC_RETURN_SERVER_RELEASE_BANNER  Set FALSE','oracle','minor','CONFIG','The information about patch/update release number provides information about the exact   patch/update release that is currently running on the database. This is sensitive   information that should not be revealed to anyone who requests it.Allowing the database to return information about the patch/update release number could   facilitate unauthorized users\' attempts to gain access based upon known patch weaknesses.The value of this parameter should be FALSE.      CIS Oracle Database   2.2.15','','SELECT count(*)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_RETURN_SERVER_RELEASE_BANNER\'  and UPPER(VALUE) =\'FALSE\'','== 1','','SELECT UPPER(VALUE)   FROM V$SYSTEM_PARAMETER   WHERE UPPER(NAME)=\'SEC_RETURN_SERVER_RELEASE_BANNER\'','The SEC_RETURN_SERVER_RELEASE_BANNER parameter value is acceptable\r','The SEC_RETURN_SERVER_RELEASE_BANNER parameter value is  not  acceptable. The parameter must be  FALSE','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(79,'AA_Oracle_270_Default Accounts Password Changed','oracle','critical','ACCOUNT','This test checks whether passwords have been changed for all Oracle default accounts.  It uses an Oracle view that was introduced in Oracle11gR1 to determine whether default passwords for well known accounts have been changed.  The test only checks default passwords for accounts with a OPEN or EXPIRED status.  It is important to change the default passwords for these well known accounts as it may provide unauthorized access to your server.   CIS 1.2','','SELECT count(*)     FROM DBA_USERS_WITH_DEFPWD A, DBA_USERS B    WHERE     A.USERNAME NOT LIKE \'%XS$NULL%\'          AND A.USERNAME = B.USERNAME          AND B.ACCOUNT_STATUS != \'EXPIRED & LOCKED\'','== 0','','SELECT B.USERNAME||\'  \'||B.ACCOUNT_STATUS     FROM DBA_USERS_WITH_DEFPWD A, DBA_USERS B    WHERE     A.USERNAME NOT LIKE \'%XS$NULL%\'          AND A.USERNAME = B.USERNAME          AND B.ACCOUNT_STATUS NOT LIKE \'%EXPIRED%LOCKED%\' ','Default accounts password are changed.\r','Default accounts password are not changed. Defaults accounts passwords must be changed','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(80,'AA_Oracle_280_11_No Authorization To AUDIT SYSTEM Privilege','oracle','major','AUDIT','This test checks for grants of system privilege \'AUDIT SYSTEM\' to unauthorized users. As assignment of the \'AUDIT SYSTEM\' privilege can allow the unauthorized alteration of the system audit activities and disabling the creation of audit trails. This capability should be restricted. This test excludes privileges granted to these system predefined grantees (\'DBA\', \'DATAPUMP_IMP_FULL_DATABASE\', \'IMP_FULL_DATABASE\', \'SYS\', \'AUDIT_ADMIN\'). Grantee with DBA roles is also excluded.   CIS: 5.2.7','','SELECT count(*)   FROM DBA_SYS_PRIVS   WHERE PRIVILEGE=\'AUDIT SYSTEM\'   AND GRANTEE NOT IN  (   \'MF_DBSPI\',   \'ANONYMOUS\',   \'CTXSYS\',   \'DBSNMP\',   \'EXFSYS\',   \'LBACSYS\',   \'MDSYS\',   \'MGMT_VIEW\',   \'OLAP