H_ADMIN\',   \'DV_MONITOR\',   \'DV_STREAMS_ADMIN\',   \'DV_GOLDENGATE_ADMIN\',   \'DV_XSTREAM_ADMIN\',   \'DV_GOLDENGATE_REDO_ACCESS\',   \'DV_AUDIT_CLEANUP\',   \'DV_DATAPUMP_NETWORK_LINK\',   \'DV_POLICY_OWNER\',   \'GSMADMIN_INTERNAL\'   )   AND OWNER not like \'APEX%\'   AND TABLE_NAME NOT LIKE (\'TOAD_PLAN%\')   ','There is no any object privilege which is granted to PUBLIC role\r','There are some object privileges which are granted to PUBLIC role. Revoke all these privileges','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(107,'AA_Oracle_440_12_object privileges granted to PUBLIC role','oracle','critical','PRIV','Permissions on objects may be granted to the user group PUBLIC. Because every database user is a member of the PUBLIC group, granting object permissions to PUBLIC gives all users in the database access to that object. In a secure environment, granting object permissions to PUBLIC should be restricted to those objects that all users are allowed to access. The policy does not require object permissions assigned to PUBLIC by the installation of Oracle Database server components be revoked. Object permissions granted to PUBLIC should be restricted.','','SELECT count(*)     FROM dba_tab_privs where grantee =\'PUBLIC\'             AND OWNER NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                FROM DBA_USERS                               WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')          AND OWNER NOT IN (SELECT ROLE                                FROM DBA_ROLES                               WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')          AND TABLE_NAME NOT IN (\'TOAD_PLAN_TABLE\', \'TOAD_PLAN_SQL\')         AND OWNER NOT LIKE \'APEX%\'','== 0','','select  \'OWNER :\'||OWNER||\' TABLE NAME : \'||TABLE_NAME     FROM dba_tab_privs where grantee =\'PUBLIC\'             AND OWNER NOT IN (SELECT USERNAME                                FROM DBA_USERS                               WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')          AND OWNER NOT IN (SELECT ROLE                                FROM DBA_ROLES                               WHERE ORACLE_MAINTAINED = \'Y\')          AND TABLE_NAME NOT IN (\'TOAD_PLAN_TABLE\',\'TOAD_PLAN_SQL\')          AND OWNER NOT LIKE \'APEX%\'','There is no any object privilege which is granted to PUBLIC role\r','There are some object privileges which are granted to PUBLIC role. Revoke all these privileges','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(108,'AA_Oracle_450_Oracle audit table ownership','oracle','major','AUDIT','Audit data is frequently targeted by malicious users as it can provide means to detect their activity. The protection of the audit trail data is of special concern and requires restrictions to allow only the auditor and DBMS backup, recovery, and maintenance users access to it. The audit table should be owned by SYS or SYSTEM.','','SELECT COUNT (*)     FROM dba_tables    WHERE table_name = \'AUD$\' AND owner not IN (\'SYS\', \'SYSTEM\')','== 0','','select OWNER from dba_tables where table_name =\'AUD$\'  and owner not  in ( \'SYS\',\'SYSTEM\')','AUD$ table is in correct schema\r','AUD$ table is not in correct schema. Drop and move AUD$ table to SYS or SYSTEM user','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(109,'AA_Oracle_460_Minimum SYSDBA privilege assignment','oracle','critical','ACCOUNT','Oracle SYSDBA privileges include privileges to administer the database outside of database controls (when the database is shut down or open in restricted mode). These privileges are in addition to all privileges controlled under database operation. Assignment of SYSDBA privileges in the Oracle password file to unauthorized persons can compromise all DBMS activities. ','','SELECT count(*)     FROM v$pwfile_users    WHERE     SYSDBA = \'TRUE\'          AND username NOT IN (\'SYS\',                               \'SYSTEM\',                               \'RCAKIR\',                               \'MERCAKMAK\',                               \'OELMAS\',                               \'OZENGINBA\',                               \'BGDB\',\'SRV_MXEOD\',\'OBA12609\',\'OBA12854\',\'OBA12656\')','== 0','','SELECT username     FROM v$pwfile_users    WHERE     SYSDBA = \'TRUE\'          AND username NOT IN (\'SYS\',                               \'SYSTEM\',                                \'RCAKIR\',                               \'MERCAKMAK\',                               \'OELMAS\',                               \'OZENGINBA\',                               \'BGDB\',\'SRV_MXEOD\',\'OBA12609\',\'OBA12854\', \'OBA12656\')','SYSDBA role is assigned to correct users.\r','SYSDBA role is not  assigned to correct users. Revoke the unnecessary users','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(110,'AA_Oracle_470_AUDIT_SYS_OPERATIONS parameter','oracle','critical','AUDIT','The AUDIT_SYS_OPERATIONS parameter is used to enable auditing of actions taken by the user SYS. The SYS user account is a shared account by definition and holds all privileges in the Oracle database. It is the account accessed by users connecting to the database with SYSDBA or SYSOPER privileges.','','select count(*)  from v$parameter where name = \'audit_sys_operations\' and value=\'TRUE\'','== 1','','select value from v$parameter where name = \'audit_sys_operations\'','AUDIT_SYS_OPERATIONS parameter is correctly set.\r','AUDIT_SYS_OPERATIONS parameter is not correctly set.  Set this Parameter to TRUE','Imported from CSV: tests-cvs.csv','2025-12-18 08:51:45','2026-01-11 16:33:38'),(111,'AA_Oracle_480_11_No Quota on SYSTEM and SYSAUX Tablespaces','oracle','major','CONFIG','This test checks for quota grants on SYSTEM and SYSAUX tablespaces.  The Oracle SYSTEM and SYSAUX tablespace is used by the database to store all DBMS system objects. Other uses of the system tablespace may compromise system availability and the effectiveness of host system access controls to the tablespace file